    {
      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_8d79fcd0249985aa81d5a86a544aeb393cf55a3500aae5d89120f077146f3b23",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "Mellin transformation transports multiplicative convolution into multiplication, so pairing a function with its conjugate-reflected partner produces the reported real positive transform on the critical line: a convolution-square positivity certificate. The displayed inverse-Mellin identity places the symmetrized Li test function in this pattern, and invariance of the explicit formula under the involution connects its sign to Weil's positivity framework. Li's gain is a simple explicit family for verification; the restricted family does not visibly exhaust Weil's broader class, and this span does not supply the separate proof mechanism that makes Li's family sufficient.",
