    {
      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_c17c926ef224c59817a34ed80d437229a3e281f9cbdfc6b46fd6b3768a212ae6",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "Inverse Mellin transformation turns the rational expression associated with a Li summand into a concrete test object in the multiplicative variable: it is supported on one side of the multiplicative identity, polynomial in the logarithm there, and separately prescribed at the boundary. This representation gains visible support and piecewise structure from an abstract transform expression, but the damaged display prevents formula-level evaluation. Within this span the mechanism is algebraic expansion of the transform; no admissibility or truncation conclusion is established here.",
