    {
      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_cec65daf8e0bfc68e6286fc616b0b24d2501c9f9c3bcdef3875df199e070f023",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "The paragraph treats the explicit formula as admitting different organizing viewpoints: Guinand foregrounds summation from self-reciprocal transforms, whereas Weil foregrounds arithmetic. Restating Weil's zeta formula in Mellin form is therefore a change of coordinates and emphasis, not yet the arithmetic translation itself. The gain is an explicitly multiplicative transform language; the burden remains to state and justify the formula, especially because the cited Guinand versions are reported either under RH or as formal and requiring case-by-case investigation.",
