      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_0e63a13112eefe9b3a01b2d2160b7b1f720c44cb91ce32d1855784ebbfb9e96c",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The paper reaches Li coefficients through two linked analytic representations: the regularized explicit-formula route produces an arithmetic expression involving prime-side data, while the concluding local-series route compares the resulting prime-sum constants with Stieltjes-type Laurent and Taylor coefficients and reports a direct derivation after the same conformal substitution. The routes meet at the coefficient sequence but carry different proof burdens.",
