    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_17e5b9287e888a61b84ea5a1d52a613b1b2ed0736eb7b2cfb313b5db34bd3730",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Li's coefficient is connected from its completed-function and symmetric-zero-set definitions to arithmetic data by a staged test-function construction: inverse Mellin transformation produces the one-sided logarithmic-polynomial test object, the explicit formula is applied only after an admissible truncation, and prime-number-theorem and zero-free-region estimates justify removing that cutoff so the regularized zero side returns the intended symmetric coefficient.",
