    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_7339c421fe2ec8208aa735c075ba31aa19ac22dbc65f29465050dea7a6c78be6",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The general transformed-multiset theorem and functional-equation symmetry establish that positivity of the concrete Li sequence is sufficient for critical-line containment, while the concluding Mellin-convolution construction explains the sign condition as a convolution-square positivity certificate of the same kind used in Weil's broader explicit-formula criterion. Thus the simple Li family inherits Weil's critical-line meaning without needing to represent every admissible Weil test function.",
